+    merge onto the line, conflicts with (#674). Empty when ``head`` does not merge cleanly
+    onto ``pre`` (the line before the first of them) either: it conflicts with earlier-wave
+    work, which is not held. Otherwise each kept bundle is tried on its own (``pre``, then
+    that bundle, then ``head``); one conflicting only with several of them together names
+    them all. The trials never move the line (:func:`_trial`)."""
